<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's Pacific Power says wind farm approved.</title>
<headline>Australia's Pacific Power says wind farm approved.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Power, one of New South Wales' three electricity generators, said on Tuesday it has been given council approval to build the state's first wind farm near Crookwell, 225 km south of Sydney.</p>
<p>Construction of the five megawatt farm, comprising eight 600 kilowatt wind turbines, would start later this year, and it was expected to be connected to the grid by mid-1988.</p>
<p>Pacific Power said distributor Great Southern Energy had agreed to buy the wind-generated electricity, sufficient to meet the average demand of 3,500 homes.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
